rows.en:
Then I heard crying coming from behind the stall door where the plant had been.
What could it be?
I opened the door.{p}

"Ah, Hosoda!"
Without waiting for {f:my|my} answer, he walked out of the club room.
{f:We|We} hurried after him.{p}

"Uh, um, I'd better not."
I answered nervously.
Then Takeuchi looked a little disappointed and went off somewhere.{p}

So the next day, I went to his classroom.
His classroom was on the first floor, so on my way back from P.E., I peeked in through the window.
Takeuchi wasn't there.{p}

"Um... I like coffee."
When I said it timidly, Takeuchi called the kitchen on the intercom for me.
What an incredible house, right?{p}

"Oh, then, I'll have some."
I tried drinking the tea.
And the taste...{p}

A big black caterpillar was squirming around inside.
"Augh☆"
{f:I|I} flung the container away.{p}

When I looked, a bug that had crawled out of the dropped container was on {f:my|my} foot...!
{f:Oh no|Oh no}.
{f:I'd|I'd} been bitten by the bug Sanbura tea is made from{f:!|!}
I hurriedly shook my foot and brushed the bug off.
But on {f:my|my} sock, little red specks of blood were welling up...{p}

Sure, I was scared, but I couldn't beat my curiosity.
I finally drank the tea.
But the taste was...{p}

Takeuchi headed for the restroom at the very end of the old school building's first floor.
I followed him in silence.
When we got to the restroom, he took something out of one of the stalls.{p}

"Takeuchi, this is amazing.
It's like the garbage in my body got sucked out...
Somehow, I feel like my body's gotten lighter."{p}

"{a}{f:|}, want to touch it?
Don't worry, it absolutely won't move."
With that, he brought the flower right up in front of {f:me|me}.{p}

"{f:Waaah|Eeek}☆"
{f:I|I} thought my heart was going to stop.
All of a sudden, the flower had started to sway{f:.|...}
Hosoda had shaken it on purpose to tease {f:me|me}{f:.|, hadn't he?}{p}

"Either you don't believe my story, or you don't understand my suffering... it's one or the other.
Don't come crying to me. There's no telling when this misfortune might strike you."
With that, Hosoda put the flower away as if it were something precious.{p}

(Takeuchi must know something about that plant.)
Convinced of that, I decided to look into the plant.
Once I'd made sure Takeuchi had gone inside the school building, I immediately doubled back.{p}

Takeuchi, too, seemed to have neutralized the poison; his face was back to normal.
And he was starting to fill the dug-up ground back in.
But I wondered why there had been maggots in the soil, so I peeked over Takeuchi's back into the hole he'd dug.{p}

A hand jutting out of the ground was gripping my foot.
I kicked at the hand with my other foot, trying to get away.
But that foot got grabbed too, and there was nothing I could do.{p}

"Gyaah☆"
{f:Hosoda|It struck him, and}{f:| Hosoda} collapsed, blood spurting from his head.
The instant the flowerpot shattered, the flower that had been biting {f:my|my} hand withered away too.{p}
